1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,977
For decades, a story has circulated

2
00:00:02,977 --> 00:00:04,800
around a small town in northern New

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,077
Mexico.

4
00:00:06,077 --> 00:00:08,248
A military facility that,

5
00:00:08,248 --> 00:00:10,977
officially, does not exist.

6
00:00:10,977 --> 00:00:13,473
Miles of tunnels underground.

7
00:00:13,473 --> 00:00:14,912
Seven levels.

8
00:00:14,912 --> 00:00:16,271
Laboratories.

9
00:00:16,271 --> 00:00:18,082
Restricted zones.

10
00:00:18,082 --> 00:00:20,508
And, according to some accounts,

11
00:00:20,508 --> 00:00:21,971
something that should never have been

12
00:00:21,971 --> 00:00:23,086
there at all.

13
00:00:23,086 --> 00:00:24,502
But much of what we now call

14
00:00:24,502 --> 00:00:27,382
the Dulce Base legend traces back to

15
00:00:27,382 --> 00:00:29,483
a single man's testimony.

16
00:00:29,483 --> 00:00:30,923
The name attached to it is Thomas

17
00:00:30,923 --> 00:00:32,455
Edwin Castello.

18
00:00:32,455 --> 00:00:35,162
And he claimed he worked inside.

19
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:38,892
Castello said he was a security

20
00:00:38,892 --> 00:00:39,925
specialist.

21
00:00:39,925 --> 00:00:41,608
In the account attributed to him,

22
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:43,385
that career eventually brought him to an

23
00:00:43,385 --> 00:00:45,625
underground installation near Dulce,

24
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:46,786
New Mexico.

25
00:00:46,786 --> 00:00:48,389
At first, none of it had to

26
00:00:48,389 --> 00:00:49,469
look alien.

27
00:00:49,469 --> 00:00:51,350
Classified facilities.

28
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,731
Staff with different levels of

29
00:00:52,731 --> 00:00:53,567
clearance.

30
00:00:53,567 --> 00:00:54,949
Controlled doors.

31
00:00:54,949 --> 00:00:55,982
Cameras.

32
00:00:55,982 --> 00:00:57,816
Identification systems.

33
00:00:57,816 --> 00:00:58,826
Secrets.

34
00:00:58,826 --> 00:01:00,765
All of it fits comfortably inside the

35
00:01:00,765 --> 00:01:03,076
world of military security.

36
00:01:03,076 --> 00:01:06,013
But Dulce, Castello said,

37
00:01:06,013 --> 00:01:07,511
was different.

38
00:01:07,511 --> 00:01:10,030
Because the deeper you went… the less

39
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:12,737
human the facility seemed.

40
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,307
He described a structure divided into

41
00:01:16,307 --> 00:01:18,269
several underground levels.

42
00:01:18,269 --> 00:01:19,476
Getting in

43
00:01:19,476 --> 00:01:21,334
wasn't just a matter of carrying the

44
00:01:21,334 --> 00:01:22,659
right badge.

45
00:01:23,064 --> 00:01:25,618
Every zone required its own clearance.

46
00:01:25,618 --> 00:01:27,220
Some employees could enter certain

47
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:28,300
areas.

48
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,494
Others, even while working inside the

49
00:01:30,494 --> 00:01:33,176
same facility, were never supposed to

50
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:35,245
know those areas existed.

51
00:01:35,556 --> 00:01:38,053
Elevators linked one section to the

52
00:01:38,053 --> 00:01:38,983
next.

53
00:01:39,388 --> 00:01:41,756
Corridors that seemed to go on forever

54
00:01:41,756 --> 00:01:44,914
connected laboratories, offices,

55
00:01:44,914 --> 00:01:48,306
technical spaces and security posts.

56
00:01:48,827 --> 00:01:50,940
And some levels were guarded far more

57
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,567
heavily than others.

58
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,804
To someone whose job was security,

59
00:01:55,804 --> 00:01:57,443
that meant one thing:

60
00:01:57,755 --> 00:01:59,429
whatever mattered most

61
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:02,610
was further down.

62
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,313
But the strangest part of his story

63
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:07,950
wasn't the doors.

64
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:10,030
It was who walked behind them.

65
00:02:10,411 --> 00:02:12,048
According to the interview attributed to

66
00:02:12,048 --> 00:02:15,218
Castello, humans were not the only ones

67
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,599
inside.

68
00:02:16,599 --> 00:02:19,351
He spoke of small grey beings.

69
00:02:19,351 --> 00:02:20,710
And of others

70
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:23,868
he described as reptilian.

71
00:02:23,868 --> 00:02:26,596
He didn't describe them as prisoners.

72
00:02:26,596 --> 00:02:28,001
In his telling,

73
00:02:28,001 --> 00:02:29,742
some of them worked there.

74
00:02:29,742 --> 00:02:31,600
They shared certain areas with human

75
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,646
staff.

76
00:02:32,958 --> 00:02:35,420
They took part in technical work.

77
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:37,440
Their presence, he claimed,

78
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,704
was simply part of how Dulce ran

79
00:02:39,704 --> 00:02:42,155
from one day to the next.

80
00:02:42,467 --> 00:02:45,358
For Castello, the impossible had become

81
00:02:45,358 --> 00:02:47,043
routine.

82
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:50,514
Try to imagine working somewhere like

83
00:02:50,514 --> 00:02:51,315
that.

84
00:02:51,315 --> 00:02:52,627
On the first day,

85
00:02:52,627 --> 00:02:54,751
it would be impossible to ignore.

86
00:02:54,751 --> 00:02:57,863
But after weeks… after months…

87
00:02:57,863 --> 00:03:00,661
even the extraordinary can start to feel

88
00:03:00,661 --> 00:03:01,880
ordinary.

89
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:04,341
That may be the most unsettling part

90
00:03:04,341 --> 00:03:05,481
of his account.

91
00:03:05,816 --> 00:03:08,196
Castello doesn't describe every shift as

92
00:03:08,196 --> 00:03:09,659
a horror film.

93
00:03:09,659 --> 00:03:11,435
He describes a job.

94
00:03:11,435 --> 00:03:12,538
Shifts.

95
00:03:12,538 --> 00:03:13,908
Procedures.

96
00:03:13,908 --> 00:03:15,324
Restrictions.

97
00:03:15,324 --> 00:03:17,149
People coming and going.

98
00:03:17,403 --> 00:03:19,505
Systems that had to keep running.

99
00:03:19,505 --> 00:03:20,607
And beings that,

100
00:03:20,607 --> 00:03:21,896
as he told it,

101
00:03:21,896 --> 00:03:24,789
were simply part of the place.

102
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:28,492
But perhaps the hardest part didn't

103
00:03:28,492 --> 00:03:30,535
happen inside Dulce.

104
00:03:30,535 --> 00:03:33,056
It happened when Thomas went home.

105
00:03:33,368 --> 00:03:35,005
According to his account,

106
00:03:35,005 --> 00:03:37,524
he was required to stay silent about

107
00:03:37,524 --> 00:03:39,232
everything he saw there.

108
00:03:39,765 --> 00:03:41,762
Picture sitting down to dinner across

109
00:03:41,762 --> 00:03:42,830
from your wife,

110
00:03:42,830 --> 00:03:44,815
after a day in a place that,

111
00:03:44,815 --> 00:03:46,603
if your story were true,

112
00:03:46,603 --> 00:03:48,635
would change everything she believes

113
00:03:48,635 --> 00:03:50,109
about the world.

114
00:03:50,109 --> 00:03:52,849
Watching her talk about ordinary things.

115
00:03:52,849 --> 00:03:54,115
The family.

116
00:03:54,115 --> 00:03:55,020
Work.

117
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,344
Tomorrow.

118
00:03:56,344 --> 00:03:58,828
And knowing that a few miles away,

119
00:03:58,828 --> 00:04:01,232
there is another reality you can never

120
00:04:01,232 --> 00:04:02,497
share with her.

121
00:04:02,497 --> 00:04:04,796
Not because you don't want to.

122
00:04:04,796 --> 00:04:07,257
Because revealing classified information

123
00:04:07,257 --> 00:04:09,300
could carry consequences.

124
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,961
For your job.

125
00:04:10,961 --> 00:04:12,122
For you.

126
00:04:12,122 --> 00:04:14,316
And, at least from the point of

127
00:04:14,316 --> 00:04:16,371
view of someone living under that kind

128
00:04:16,371 --> 00:04:18,994
of secrecy, perhaps for the people you

129
00:04:18,994 --> 00:04:20,262
love most.

130
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:22,617
So Thomas did something that,

131
00:04:22,617 --> 00:04:24,335
by his own account,

132
00:04:24,335 --> 00:04:26,612
grew harder every day.

133
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,621
He came home…

134
00:04:28,933 --> 00:04:31,640
and pretended he knew nothing.

135
00:04:32,044 --> 00:04:33,472
The next morning,

136
00:04:33,472 --> 00:04:35,446
he drove back to Dulce.

137
00:04:35,446 --> 00:04:37,373
Back to the checkpoints.

138
00:04:37,373 --> 00:04:39,242
Back to the corridors.

139
00:04:39,242 --> 00:04:41,170
Back to the beings he claimed to

140
00:04:41,170 --> 00:04:42,447
have seen.

141
00:04:42,447 --> 00:04:46,175
And back to silence.

142
00:04:47,767 --> 00:04:49,278
There were rules.

143
00:04:49,683 --> 00:04:51,238
In certain areas,

144
00:04:51,238 --> 00:04:53,177
conversations between different groups

145
00:04:53,177 --> 00:04:54,410
were restricted.

146
00:04:54,721 --> 00:04:57,591
Some information was never to be shared.

147
00:04:57,995 --> 00:05:00,770
Some questions were better left unasked.

148
00:05:00,770 --> 00:05:02,778
And some places could not be entered

149
00:05:02,778 --> 00:05:04,624
without the right clearance.

150
00:05:04,624 --> 00:05:07,039
Castello was there to help keep that

151
00:05:07,039 --> 00:05:08,607
system in place.

152
00:05:08,607 --> 00:05:10,011
And for a while,

153
00:05:10,011 --> 00:05:12,368
it seems, he did.

154
00:05:12,368 --> 00:05:14,574
Until he began to see things he

155
00:05:14,574 --> 00:05:17,767
could no longer explain away as military

156
00:05:17,767 --> 00:05:19,371
secrets.

157
00:05:20,967 --> 00:05:22,790
Laboratories take up a large part of

158
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:23,939
his story.

159
00:05:23,939 --> 00:05:27,051
Castello spoke of biological and medical

160
00:05:27,051 --> 00:05:28,119
research.

161
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:30,081
Equipment he didn't fully understand.

162
00:05:30,081 --> 00:05:31,103
Chambers.

163
00:05:31,103 --> 00:05:32,589
Observation areas.

164
00:05:32,589 --> 00:05:34,760
Human staff working close to non-human

165
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:35,909
beings.

166
00:05:35,909 --> 00:05:37,569
At first, by his account,

167
00:05:37,569 --> 00:05:39,311
there were explanations.

168
00:05:39,311 --> 00:05:41,227
Classified research.

169
00:05:41,227 --> 00:05:43,154
Experimental medicine.

170
00:05:43,154 --> 00:05:45,162
Projects sensitive enough to justify

171
00:05:45,162 --> 00:05:46,811
extreme security.

172
00:05:46,811 --> 00:05:48,994
It was possible to work there and

173
00:05:48,994 --> 00:05:50,260
still believe that,

174
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,152
however strange it all looked,

175
00:05:52,152 --> 00:05:53,812
someone higher up knew exactly what they

176
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:54,812
were doing.

177
00:05:55,217 --> 00:05:56,891
But there was a problem.

178
00:05:57,423 --> 00:05:59,559
Castello hadn't yet seen the lower

179
00:05:59,559 --> 00:06:01,070
levels.

180
00:06:02,667 --> 00:06:05,686
Over time, other workers began to tell

181
00:06:05,686 --> 00:06:06,812
him things.

182
00:06:06,812 --> 00:06:08,124
Comments.

183
00:06:08,124 --> 00:06:09,378
Rumors.

184
00:06:09,378 --> 00:06:10,689
Warnings.

185
00:06:10,689 --> 00:06:13,000
Stories about people inside the facility

186
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,358
who didn't seem to be part of

187
00:06:14,358 --> 00:06:15,566
the staff.

188
00:06:15,566 --> 00:06:17,133
According to the account,

189
00:06:17,133 --> 00:06:19,351
one encounter mattered more than the

190
00:06:19,351 --> 00:06:20,117
rest.

191
00:06:20,117 --> 00:06:22,961
Castello spoke of a man he identified

192
00:06:22,961 --> 00:06:25,086
only as George.

193
00:06:25,086 --> 00:06:26,746
George didn't say he worked there.

194
00:06:26,746 --> 00:06:28,453
He said he had been taken there.

195
00:06:28,453 --> 00:06:30,370
Against his will.

196
00:06:31,967 --> 00:06:34,974
Until then, Castello could justify a

197
00:06:34,974 --> 00:06:36,089
great deal.

198
00:06:36,089 --> 00:06:37,621
Military secrets.

199
00:06:37,621 --> 00:06:38,643
Research.

200
00:06:38,643 --> 00:06:40,686
Classified technology.

201
00:06:40,686 --> 00:06:42,532
Even the presence of beings that,

202
00:06:42,532 --> 00:06:44,448
if his story were true,

203
00:06:44,448 --> 00:06:46,143
would upend our understanding of the

204
00:06:46,143 --> 00:06:47,074
world.

205
00:06:47,385 --> 00:06:49,893
But a person held against his will

206
00:06:49,893 --> 00:06:51,056
was different.

207
00:06:51,461 --> 00:06:53,028
That was no longer a question of

208
00:06:53,028 --> 00:06:54,539
security clearance.

209
00:06:54,944 --> 00:06:56,859
It was a moral question.

210
00:06:56,859 --> 00:06:58,914
And he began to wonder what was

211
00:06:58,914 --> 00:07:00,170
really happening

212
00:07:00,853 --> 00:07:02,826
in the parts of the facility

213
00:07:02,826 --> 00:07:05,103
he still couldn't reach.

214
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:08,337
According to his account,

215
00:07:08,337 --> 00:07:10,044
other employees started showing him

216
00:07:10,044 --> 00:07:11,181
information.

217
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,377
Documents.

218
00:07:12,377 --> 00:07:13,515
Names.

219
00:07:13,515 --> 00:07:15,036
References to people who had gone

220
00:07:15,036 --> 00:07:15,860
missing.

221
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:17,962
Fragments of a story much larger than

222
00:07:17,962 --> 00:07:19,877
the facility he walked through every

223
00:07:19,877 --> 00:07:20,864
day.

224
00:07:20,864 --> 00:07:23,221
Castello began to suspect that some of

225
00:07:23,221 --> 00:07:24,974
the subjects used in certain research

226
00:07:24,974 --> 00:07:26,704
were not there by choice.

227
00:07:26,704 --> 00:07:28,875
And then, a name started to come

228
00:07:28,875 --> 00:07:29,525
up.

229
00:07:29,525 --> 00:07:31,057
What a few of the workers called

230
00:07:31,057 --> 00:07:32,857
one of the lower areas.

231
00:07:32,857 --> 00:07:34,681
Nightmare Hall.

232
00:07:36,267 --> 00:07:37,765
According to the story,

233
00:07:37,765 --> 00:07:38,995
it lay on one of the most

234
00:07:38,995 --> 00:07:41,596
restricted levels of Dulce.

235
00:07:41,596 --> 00:07:43,964
Castello still didn't fully understand

236
00:07:43,964 --> 00:07:45,532
what was down there.

237
00:07:45,532 --> 00:07:47,447
But the warnings were enough.

238
00:07:47,447 --> 00:07:48,573
People.

239
00:07:48,573 --> 00:07:49,851
Beings.

240
00:07:49,851 --> 00:07:51,279
Containment.

241
00:07:51,279 --> 00:07:53,090
Experimentation.

242
00:07:53,090 --> 00:07:55,423
Projects that supposedly went far beyond

243
00:07:55,423 --> 00:07:57,896
any research he had seen so far.

244
00:07:57,896 --> 00:07:59,150
At some point,

245
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:01,019
he had to make a decision.

246
00:08:01,019 --> 00:08:03,318
He could keep doing his job.

247
00:08:03,318 --> 00:08:04,967
Keep his head down.

248
00:08:04,967 --> 00:08:06,801
Respect the clearances.

249
00:08:06,801 --> 00:08:09,054
And go home every night.

250
00:08:09,054 --> 00:08:10,818
Or he could find out what was

251
00:08:10,818 --> 00:08:12,562
really below.

252
00:08:14,133 --> 00:08:15,805
According to the account attributed to

253
00:08:15,805 --> 00:08:19,021
Thomas Castello… he chose to go down.

254
00:08:19,021 --> 00:08:20,321
And what he claimed to find on

255
00:08:20,321 --> 00:08:22,376
the lower levels changed his story

256
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:23,363
completely.

257
00:08:23,363 --> 00:08:24,861
Containment chambers.

258
00:08:24,861 --> 00:08:26,138
People being held.

259
00:08:26,138 --> 00:08:27,322
Experiments.

260
00:08:27,322 --> 00:08:29,528
Beings he couldn't identify.

261
00:08:29,528 --> 00:08:31,467
And the place some workers had learned

262
00:08:31,467 --> 00:08:33,777
to call Nightmare Hall.

263
00:08:33,777 --> 00:08:35,089
But that is only part of the

264
00:08:35,089 --> 00:08:35,995
problem.

265
00:08:35,995 --> 00:08:37,539
Because when we try to find out

266
00:08:37,539 --> 00:08:40,674
who Thomas Edwin Castello really was,

267
00:08:40,674 --> 00:08:42,485
an even more uncomfortable question

268
00:08:42,485 --> 00:08:43,716
appears.

269
00:08:43,716 --> 00:08:48,199
Can we prove this man ever existed?

270
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,170
In Part Two,

271
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:53,296
we go inside Nightmare Hall.

272
00:08:53,608 --> 00:08:56,162
We'll reconstruct what Castello said he

273
00:08:56,162 --> 00:08:57,139
saw there.

274
00:08:57,451 --> 00:08:59,251
What he claimed was happening to the

275
00:08:59,251 --> 00:09:00,818
people being held.

276
00:09:00,818 --> 00:09:03,453
And what, in his version of events,

277
00:09:03,453 --> 00:09:05,833
set off the conflict inside Dulce.

278
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:08,016
Then we'll step outside his story,

279
00:09:08,016 --> 00:09:09,676
to investigate something that may be

280
00:09:09,676 --> 00:09:10,837
even stranger:

281
00:09:10,837 --> 00:09:12,950
where the Dulce legend actually came

282
00:09:12,950 --> 00:09:13,739
from.

283
00:09:13,739 --> 00:09:16,677
Because Thomas Castello wasn't the

284
00:09:16,677 --> 00:09:17,770
beginning.

285
00:09:18,302 --> 00:09:20,554
Follow the story back far enough,

286
00:09:20,554 --> 00:09:22,367
and another name appears.

287
00:09:22,679 --> 00:09:24,805
Paul Bennewitz.

288
00:09:25,117 --> 00:09:26,394
And with him,

289
00:09:26,394 --> 00:09:28,948
a very different possibility.

290
00:09:28,948 --> 00:09:31,120
That part of the Dulce story didn't

291
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,689
begin with aliens…

292
00:09:33,093 --> 00:09:35,521
but with disinformation.
